        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The most common cause is the 'Static Spark' or 'Improper Grounding' during the transfer of flammable solvents into a mixing vessel. If your formulations include alcohols, hydrocarbons, or acetates, you must ensure all equipment is electrically bonded and grounded to prevent electrostatic discharge."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How can I verify a raw material if I don't have a full analytical lab?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Even a basic 'QC Desk' can perform critical checks. Measuring refractive index, specific gravity, and pH can detect over 80% of major raw material errors or dilutions. Investing in these three affordable tools is the first step for any chemical startup."
