    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can a bad formulation really destroy a stainless steel tank?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Absolutely. High chloride levels in an acidic environment (like a poorly formulated heavy-duty descaler) can cause pitting corrosion in 304 or 316 stainless steel within hours. Always check the metallurgy of your seals and vessels against the chemical compatibility charts."
      }
