      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It is the range of temperature, pressure, and mixing speed within which a reaction can be safety controlled. Moving outside this window (e.g., mixing too fast and creating cavitation) can lead to equipment fatigue and mechanical failure."
